{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":2579958,"ns":0,"title":"Augustinian hypothesis","extract":"The Augustinian hypothesis (sometimes referred to as the Augustinian Proposal) is a solution to the synoptic problem, which concerns the origin of the canonical Gospels in the New Testament. The hypothesis holds that Matthew was written first, by Matthew the Evangelist (see the Gospel According to the Hebrews and the Jewish-Christian Gospels).","description":"Theory on the origin of the synoptic Gospels","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}